Subject: [PATCH 56/56] feat(admin): the server's wave ranking of a goal can be
 read (1691)

The tester's 49931: 1691 still cannot be shown. With six candidates the
model's plan named five (it left out D, 3/10, and kept F, 0/10), and all
five went in wave 1, so the ranking never had to drop anyone. The order is
not visible through a plan the model writes.

GET /admin/goals/:id/wave-ranking returns the plan's people in the order
the waves use (rankingOf, which shares its reads with inWaveOrder), with the
signals behind each place: rank, name, named_by_goal, the pre-match word,
the field rate and the overall rate, plus the answer-stats field the rates
were read in. No phone numbers. A goal on a fictional seat only: 403 for a
real owner, 404 for no goal or no plan, 500 when a signal cannot be read
(unlike the waves, which fall back to the plan's order).

DONE WHEN: for a fictional goal with known records, the read lists the
candidates in the defined order; changing one record moves that one.

